</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grounded clustering.</span>
Figure <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5.3 Mode Averages ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Diffusion Mental Averages" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> presents our cluster averages from grounded clustering using BLIP-VQA. The results show that DMA can generate accurate average images across different grounded criteria. For the <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">car</span> concept grounded by color, the averages show that yellow and silver cars look similar, while red and blue cars form another consistent group. This demonstrates how DMA can be used as a probing tool to reveal how models organize and associate attributes within a concept.</p>
</div>
