<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F13.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="S3.F13.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:113%;">Results of the <span id="S3.F13.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">replacement baseline</span> with different <math id="S3.F13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="S3.F13.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> This baseline yields inconsistent images, even with high <math id="S3.F13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> values.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Effects of <math id="S3.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze the effects of varying the cutoff timestep <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Figure <a href="#S3.F14" title='Figure 14 ‣ C.4 Effects of 𝑡_"stop" ‣ C Ablation Studies ‣ Diffusion Mental Averages' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. The results show that a low <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}=5</annotation></semantics></math> leads to inconsistent average images, such as architectural incoherence in the <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">castle</span>, ground-plane variations in the <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">dog</span>, and costume inconsistencies in the <span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">firefighter</span>. Increasing <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> beyond 10 provides only minor improvements in visual consistency for most concepts. We therefore set <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{stop}}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{stop}}=10</annotation></semantics></math> as a balance between computational efficiency and cross-sample consistency.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F14" class="ltx_figure">
